# Cloudflare Pages security headers — apps/docs (pre-HN-launch hardening).
#
# This file is copied verbatim into the build output by Docusaurus (anything
# in `static/` lands at the site root) and consumed by Cloudflare Pages at
# request time. See: https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/
#
# Target: securityheaders.com B+ or better post-deploy.
#
# CSP notes:
#   - script-src: 'self' + Plausible Analytics (plausible.io) for usage stats.
#     Docusaurus injects its bundle from /assets/* (same-origin), which 'self'
#     covers — BUT it also emits two INLINE bootstrap scripts that 'self' does
#     NOT cover (inline needs a hash/nonce): the theme initialiser (sets
#     data-theme before paint to avoid a flash) and the base-url load-failure
#     banner. Both are allow-listed by their sha256 below. The banner hash is
#     baseUrl-dependent — regenerate both if baseUrl or the Docusaurus version
#     changes: `node -e` sha256(inline <script> bodies of build/index.html).
#     Search is `@easyops-cn/docusaurus-search-local` — a fully client-side
#     lunr index served from the site's own origin, no remote script/connect
#     needed (replaces the never-provisioned Algolia DocSearch stub).
#     https://browser.sentry-cdn.com — Sentry CDN loader for client-side error
#     tracking (injected via docusaurus.config.ts headTags when SENTRY_DSN_DOCS
#     is set at build time). Source: https://docs.sentry.io/platforms/javascript/install/cdn/#content-security-policy
#   - style-src: includes 'unsafe-inline' because Docusaurus injects inline
#     <style> blocks for the syntax highlighter and theme tokens; this is
#     the documented Docusaurus baseline and cannot be removed without
#     forking the framework. Tracked as DEBT-CSP-DOCS-INLINE-STYLE.
#   - connect-src: Plausible (analytics) +
#     https://*.ingest.sentry.io — Sentry event/error ingest from CDN loader
#     (docs has no tunnel route, so the loader POSTs directly to Sentry).
#     Source: https://docs.sentry.io/platforms/javascript/install/cdn/#content-security-policy
#     https://status.corelink.humangr.com — BetterStack badge.json fetch by
#     StatusPill component (CNAME to BetterStack; browser sees this hostname).
#     https://humangr.com — NewsletterSignup POSTs cross-origin
#     to admin-ui /api/newsletter/subscribe route.
#     https://corelink-api.humangr.com — the pilot apply form POSTs
#     cross-origin to /v1/signup/pilot/{token}. Without this entry the
#     browser refuses the fetch before it leaves the page, and the form's
#     catch branch renders a "network error" that names a host the request
#     never actually reached.
#   - img-src: data: + https: kept permissive for embedded screenshots.
#   - frame-ancestors 'none' (no embedding the docs site in iframes).
#   - no frame-src needed — docs never embeds Stripe / Clerk.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'sha256-0xt7rjlfRsoD7aukiSWSNvMBWU159Lh5cl3WNaV1g+w=' 'sha256-0ruMAFH9auSuLY3YAHGSHAcwCIo9sGOgiXNMd+7JqKQ=' https://plausible.io https://browser.sentry-cdn.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: https:; font-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' https://plausible.io https://*.ingest.sentry.io https://status.corelink.humangr.com https://humangr.com https://corelink-api.humangr.com; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; object-src 'none'
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: interest-cohort=(), camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
